From 2e3980f1ebb9a20677738083c9f311facaf606b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pkgdemon <jpm820@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:57:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] NextBSD: create no pflog0 at boot, as xnu does

FreeBSD's pflogattach() creates pflog0 when pf loads. xnu registers its
pflog cloner with a minimum of 0 interfaces, so a Mac has no pflog0 until
something creates one (checked on 10.9.5 and current macOS). Leave the
cloner registered and create nothing; `ifconfig pflog0 create` makes it
when pf logging is wanted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/netpfil/pf/if_pflog.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sys/netpfil/pf/if_pflog.c b/sys/netpfil/pf/if_pflog.c
index cb96d2fcc..99bf6e264 100644
--- a/sys/netpfil/pf/if_pflog.c
+++ b/sys/netpfil/pf/if_pflog.c
@@ -114,8 +114,12 @@ pflogattach(int npflog __unused)
 		.flags = IFC_F_AUTOUNIT,
 	};
 	V_pflog_cloner = ifc_attach_cloner(pflogname, &req);
-	struct ifc_data ifd = { .unit = 0 };
-	ifc_create_ifp(pflogname, &ifd, NULL);
+	/*
+	 * NextBSD: no pflog0 at boot, as in xnu (whose pflog cloner has a
+	 * minimum of 0 interfaces). Whoever enables pf logging creates it with
+	 * `ifconfig pflog0 create`; until then pf's log rules have nowhere to
+	 * log, which it already handles.
+	 */
 }
 
 static int
